Revision history for Red::Driver::Pg

{{$NEXT}}

0.0.3  2026-11-24T02:19:34Z
    - Select the local Red checkout consistently for direct prove6 and executor runs.
    - Require Red 0.2.16 for row security and administration support.
    - Add is global-notifiable support through PostgreSQL AFTER INSERT triggers and
      pg_notify on the red_events channel.
    - Decode LISTEN payloads into Red global events so ResultSeq.Supply works across
      processes and nodes.
    - Capture and migrate notification trigger DDL in schema snapshots.
    - Use a stable DB::Pg handle for LISTEN callbacks outside transaction scopes.
    - Require Red 0.2.15 or later for the global event driver hooks.

0.0.2  2026-11-14T16:25:47Z
    - Require Red 0.2.10 or later (API 2).
    - Move PostgreSQL-specific migration, schema, regex rendering, and driver
      support implementations from Red into this distribution.
    - Provide PostgreSQL range constructors and exclusion constraint traits
      through Red::Driver::Pg::AST and Red::Driver::Pg::Schema.
    - Validate native operators, range constructors, and range bounds.
    - Add tests for driver support, schema constraints, and regex rendering.
    - Install the Red master checkout before driver dependencies in CI so the
      test suites use the intended Red version.

0.0.1  2026-11-02T19:59:26Z
    - Restore the README and generate it from lib/Red/Driver/Pg.rakudoc.
    - Require Red 0.2.9 or later (API 2).

0.0.1
    - Extract the PostgreSQL driver from Red into a separate distribution.
    - Add driver-specific tests and isolated PostgreSQL test databases.
    - Include PostgreSQL catalog introspection through the schema reader.
    - Run the driver and upstream Red master test suites on GitHub Actions.
